  "description": "meme-id: banner_in_the_streets_hulk_in_the_sheets; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a photo of actor Mark Ruffalo with the text 'banner in the streets' and a photo of the Hulk with the text 'hulk in the sheets,' creating a pun on the phrase 'in the sheets' (meaning in bed) versus 'in the streets' (meaning in public). The intent is to humorously suggest that Ruffalo, who plays the Hulk, is so associated with the character that he is 'in the sheets' (i.e., in bed) while the Hulk is 'in the streets' (i.e., in public). This is a lighthearted, self-referential joke about the actor's role and does not target any protected group or contain abusive, hateful, or propagandistic content. However, the phrase 'in the sheets' can be interpreted as a crude euphemism for sexual activity, which may be considered mildly offensive or inappropriate in some contexts, making the meme potentially harmful due to its suggestive nature, though not malicious or targeted.",
